  "note": "Complete permanent Budapest Keleti passenger building: monumental pale classical west entrance with recessed arched glazing, clock, paired columns, niches and parapet; full long barrel-roof nave and raised pale-green rooflight; both front mansard pavilions, central and rear side pavilions, low yellow ranges and open courtyard spaces. Preserve the underground metro/plaza relation, independent city blocks, roads, rails and eastern approach ground. No copied lettering, brands, figurative statuary, people, trains or navigable interior. Preserve native31.4m front,31m nave,14m pavilions and8m low ranges. Source nave eaves18.5m/crown31m,raised rooflight32m and original non-figurative crest34.4m are architectural controls. Closed occupied floor+.85m and foundation-6.5m share one unchanged host terrain datum. Side pavilions have two storeys; low ranges one storey. Four photo/inferred court voids stay open in roof, floor and ground masks. No per-part host offsets or invented metro-plaza floor. One common unchanged global-field sample[-100,4],114.10798140000001m,suppliesY=0. Exact nativecontact requires currentfield review. No per-part hostoffsets,blanket parent floor or artificial metroplaza. Preview uses the host terrain sample at the authored base; ground slope, facade azimuth and final site fit remain review items."
